  "id": "COMPOUND:29799 - PROTEIN:5840",
  "verbalization": "The compound in question, (2R,3R,4S,5S,6R)-2-[[(5R,6R)-9-(3,4-dihydroxyphenyl)-2,3,5-trihydroxy-6,7-dihydro-5H-benzo[7]annulen-6-yl]oxy]-6-(hydroxymethyl)oxane-3,4,5-triol, is shown to interact with H9 through multiple pathways. It is a target of two distinct compounds: Erysimoside and Dehydrogenase/reductase SDR family member 9, both of which are themselves targets of H9. Additionally, the compound is linked to Lysine-specific demethylase 4D-like, which is also a target of Dendridine A, which in turn targets H9. This suggests that the compound may act through a series of enzymatic pathways that ultimately lead to the activation or modulation of H9. The evidence points to a potential role of the compound in influencing H9 through interactions with enzymes in the SDR family and the demethylase pathway, though the exact mechanism of action remains to be fully elucidated.",
